   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "PICTURES\n\nA picture is a PAD -- the\nsame tablet you write words\non, with an image on its\nface.\n\nSo it copies, files into a\nnotebook, goes in a box,\nand Dusty takes it away,\nexactly as a word does.\nNone of that was written\nagain for pictures."
   },
   "x": -1.45,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TO TRY IT\n\nDrag an image file from\nyour machine onto the page:\nit lands as a pad WHERE YOU\nDROPPED IT.\n\nDrop it on a pad that is\nalready there and the\npicture covers that pad\ninstead.\n\nHold one and press Ctrl and\nthe up arrow to make it\nbigger; a picture keeps its\nown proportions."
   },
   "x": -0.75,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "WORDS ON A PICTURE\n\nTwo of these say something.\nPick one up and type: the\nwords are drawn over the\npicture, on the one pad.\n\nWhich matters for robots. A\nthought that holds a picture\nmatches that picture and no\nother -- see naming.world.\nThe words count too, so a\ncaptioned picture and a bare\none are different things."
   },
